NOTE PROBLEM

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.300
A barbershop takes money all day.

2
00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:11.500
It lands in a till, in one currency, and sits there —
idle until somebody moves it by hand.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.700
We wanted the till to become a portfolio,
and the portfolio to still spend.

NOTE LIVE SETTLEMENT ON SEPOLIA

4
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:23.400
So we built UNICA: a settlement hook for Uniswap v4,
live and source-verified on Ethereum Sepolia.

5
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:31.500
One disclosure first — the specification and threat model
were written before the event; every line of code
was written during it.

6
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.000
Here is the settlement that ran.
The payer sent one thousandth of an ETH.

7
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.400
The merchant received exactly 2.003660 USDC —
not about, exactly.

8
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:50.400
Uniswap did the conversion: the swap's sender is
Uniswap's own Universal Router, and our hook admits no other.

9
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.800
The order is Settled, and paying it again reverts.

NOTE VERIFICATION

10
00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.100
You do not have to trust that receipt.
Our verifier rebuilds it.

11
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.900
The quote digest is recomputed
from the quote's own fields.

12
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:10.500
The merchant's address is recovered from a signature
over that rebuilt digest.

13
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.100
The pool id is rebuilt from the whole pool key.
Only then is anything compared with the log.

14
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:21.400
Thirty-seven checks, and nothing is read back
and agreed with.

NOTE TREASURY — BEING BUILT

15
00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:26.000
The portfolio half is being built.
Here is where it stands.

16
00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:34.400
On Circle's Arc we read the live chain and modelled
a merchant treasury: a reserve floor, a per-action cap,
one permitted transfer.

17
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.400
Twenty live reads,
a hundred and seventy-seven offline rows.

18
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.800
No UNICA contract exists on Arc.
We broadcast nothing there.

19
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.400
The tool renders the transaction
an owner would sign, then stops.

NOTE CONFIDENTIAL STRATEGY

20
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:56.200
The strategy above it is confidential.
This is a Chainlink CRE Confidential Workflow,
registered with handlerInTee.

21
00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.700
Five private policy values
load inside the handler.

22
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:09.300
What leaves it is a policy commitment, an action class
and a reason category — no threshold reaches
any published field.

23
00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:17.100
That run just happened: exit zero,
"Handler requested TEE Execution",
evidence grade CRE_CONFIDENTIAL_SIMULATION.

24
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.500
Chainlink's own CLI says plainly
that this simulator is not a real TEE.

25
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:24.100
Nothing here has run in an enclave.

NOTE STATUS

26
00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:29.400
Where each piece stands.
Uniswap: live, one settlement receipted.

27
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.400
Chainlink: simulated,
deploy access pending review.

28
00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:39.000
ENSv2: seventy-eight live Sepolia reads —
and we own no ENS name.

29
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:44.100
The Graph: written, never deployed;
no live read has ever been observed.

30
00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:49.800
Arc: nothing broadcast. And V2 is frozen at release
candidate one, and blocked, by a Critical
we found and published ourselves.

NOTE CLOSE

31
00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:55.100
A merchant's till becomes a portfolio —
and the portfolio still spends.

32
00:02:55.100 --> 00:03:00.400
Exact settlement today. Merchant-controlled treasury
automation is being built.
UNICA, by NFTeria: independent, MIT-licensed.
